	"version": 1,
	"about": "Renderer data for RLHeadPortraitMap: how a Human's saved appearance (PortraitCustomization PC/1-PC/2 fields and palette indices) becomes the RL head at High. Changing it changes every Human at High equally (players, NPCs, legacy saves); it is never sent on the wire.",
	"controls": {
		"about": "x = clamp(gain * (v - c) / 50, -cap, cap), c = the field's value in HumanPortraitPresets Rowan (male) / Mira (female). Gains per body sex from tests/rl_head_gain_probe.gd (2026-10-27): |gain| matches the RL control's displacement per slider unit to the Low/Medium sculpt's near the centre (95th-percentile magnitudes, mean of both directions); eye_size and its eyelid coupling by joint least squares. eye_tilt is negative: RL eye_tilt + raises the inner corners, the Low/Medium slider the outer ones. Secondary couplings are the plan's (jaw, nose, face_length, brow_depth) and the probe's (eye_size -> eyelid).",
